# Description: Select an application by name (AID); EDIT the AID bytes first.
# Category: templates
#
# WHAT THIS DOES
# Selects an application on the card by its application identifier (AID),
# also called the DF name. This is how you "enter" an application such as a
# payment, ID, or loyalty application before sending the commands it
# understands.
#
# !!! EDIT BEFORE USE !!!
# The AID below (A0 00 00 00 04 10 10) is only an EXAMPLE. Replace the
# seven AID bytes with an application identifier that is valid for your
# card: for example one you saw in the output of the read_ef_dir script,
# one from the card's documentation, or one from its specification. Then
# adjust Lc (the byte that says how many AID bytes follow, here 07) so it
# always equals the number of AID bytes you entered.
#
# THE COMMAND, BYTE BY BYTE
#   00                   class byte: standard interindustry commands
#   A4                   instruction: SELECT FILE
#   04                   P1 = 4: select by DF name (the AID)
#   00                   P2 = 0: first or only occurrence, no control info
#   07                   Lc: exactly 7 data bytes follow
#   A0 00 00 00 04 10 10 EXAMPLE AID - replace with your card's own AID
#
# WHAT YOU SHOULD SEE
#   SW 90 00 or 61 XX    the application was selected
#   SW 6A 82             no application with that AID exists on the card
#
# Selecting an application does not by itself modify the card, but the
# selected application decides which commands it accepts next.
00 A4 04 00 07 A0 00 00 00 04 10 10
